  "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)\u2248f(a,b,c)+\u2207f(a,b,c)\\cdot \u27e8x-a,y-b,z-c\u27e9.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & \u2248f(3,2,1)+\u2207f(3,2,1)\\cdot \u27e8x-3,y-2,z-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =12+\u27e8{f}_{x}(3,2,1),{f}_{y}(3,2,1),{f}_{z}(3,2,1)\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-3,y-2,z-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =12+\u27e84,12,36\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-3,y-2,z-1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(2.97,2.1,1.04)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=2.97,$ $y=2.1,$ and $z=1.04$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.97,2.1,1.04) & \u224812+\u27e84,12,36\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82.97-3,2.1-2,1.04-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =12+\u27e84,12,36\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-0.03,0.1,0.04\u27e9 \\\\  & =12+4(-0.03)+12(0.1)+36(0.04) \\\\  & =12-0.12+1.2+1.44 \\\\  & =14.52\\end{aligned}\n$$",
